<title>HONG KONG: HK April orders on hand fall 10 pct yr on yr.</title>
<headline>HK April orders on hand fall 10 pct yr on yr.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Census and Statistics Department said April orders-on-hand fell 10 percent in value on the year against a revised 10 percent drop in March.</p>
<p>The following are provisional percentage changes in the value of orders-on-hand in April 1997 over April 1996 (* means that comparative figure has been revised and *** means that the change is within +/- 0.5 percent):</p>
<p>						  April 1997  March 1997</p>
<p> All industries covered in the survey -10	    -10*</p>
<p> Wearing apparel			     -4	     -4</p>
<p> Textiles					-8	     -9</p>
<p>						  April 1997  March 1997</p>
<p> Electronic Products			-16	    -16</p>
<p> Electrical products			 -3	     -9</p>
<p> Fabricated metal products		-18	     -9</p>
<p> Plastic products			   -17	    -17</p>
<p> Printing and publishing		   +9	     -1</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6441.  http://www.hk97.com</p>
</text>
